Round-3 paper batch 2, code: stage block U with the upsert cells and H-a per definition writer

analysis.ex_round3_upsert (exploratory, no model call): per changed item-time, whether the B=0
delta derivation yielded a new item for the slot since the fork, with Update of B=0, the upsert and
B=1 on each part, each part's share of binding's effect and the answers the upsert moved.
round3_paper: block U stages the refresh and upsert runs (U1-U4; U5 needs the M2 families), block
H is staged per definition-item writer (h_sonnet.json with its response-cache snapshot; a later
writer is one more H_WRITERS entry), u_delta.json; RThree macros for U3, U4, the delta split and
H1, H2; tab_round3 gains U3, U4, H1, H2 and the upsert levels. Unit tests on hand-built inputs.

